I compared it to \( \int_{1}^{\pi/2} \frac{1}{x^m} \, dx \), but actually, since \( 1 - \cos(x) \leq 2 \), the integrand is bounded by \( \frac{2}{x^m} \). So, if \( \int_{1}^{\pi/2} \frac{1}{x^m} \, dx \) converges, then the original integral converges.

