$$

For each $x \in [-4, 0]$, the term $|(x - x_0) \cdot (x - x_1) \cdot \ldots \cdot (x - x_n)|$ is a product of $n+1$ terms, each of the maximum distance from any node. We need to obtain an upper bound for this product. To find the largest possible value of this product over the interval $[-4, 0]$, we can consider a midpoint or evaluate the Lyapunov coefficient.

